  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "34676048",
      "title": "Extracting Session Data & Rendering Conditional User Interfaces",
      "lectureOrder": 97,
      "videoOrder": 90,
      "sourceHash": "d26db4d57e3ce73fb9574b8104e9a89955cd1fa0cc741f268c2b792f48a439dc",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 5.4,
          "en": "So here in this marketing area, I wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.4,
          "end": 8.939,
          "en": "that this login button in the navigation bar is not shown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.939,
          "end": 13.53,
          "en": "if we are logged in because it makes no sense to get us back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.53,
          "end": 15.51,
          "en": "to the login page in that case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.51,
          "end": 16.62,
          "en": "But instead, I wanna show",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.62,
          "end": 20.07,
          "en": "let's say a log out button In that case, which sounds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.07,
          "end": 21.213,
          "en": "like a better idea.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.29,
          "end": 23.37,
          "en": "To achieve this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.37,
          "end": 25.74,
          "en": "we have to find out in our front and code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.74,
          "end": 28.83,
          "en": "whether the user is login or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.83,
          "end": 30.06,
          "en": "And we can find out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.06,
          "end": 33.06,
          "en": "by checking for the existence of this session cookie.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.06,
          "end": 35.97,
          "en": "However, with front and JavaScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.97,
          "end": 38.34,
          "en": "we don't have access to this cookie.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 38.34,
          "end": 40.11,
          "en": "We created it such that front",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.11,
          "end": 43.8,
          "en": "and JavaScript code can't read the cookie.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.8,
          "end": 45.96,
          "en": "But what we can do instead is we can go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 45.96,
          "end": 48.15,
          "en": "to our marketing jsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 48.15,
          "end": 50.46,
          "en": "So this layout route here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 50.46,
          "end": 53.103,
          "en": "and there we could export a loader,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 54.21,
          "end": 56.76,
          "en": "export this loader function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 56.76,
          "end": 59.88,
          "en": "as we did it multiple times before in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 59.88,
          "end": 62.22,
          "en": "And here in this loader, we could check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 62.22,
          "end": 65.67,
          "en": "whether this request that's coming in from the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 65.67,
          "end": 69.36,
          "en": "has a valid session cookie attached to it or not,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 69.36,
          "end": 70.83,
          "en": "because that's all important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 70.83,
          "end": 74.58,
          "en": "The browser will automatically attach the session cookie",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 74.58,
          "end": 77.85,
          "en": "to all requests it sends to our backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 77.85,
          "end": 80.25,
          "en": "So every request will contain that cookie.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 80.25,
          "end": 81.78,
          "en": "Hence here on the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 81.78,
          "end": 85.5,
          "en": "we just need to extract it and validated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 85.5,
          "end": 89.37,
          "en": "To do that, we can go back to the off server JS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 89.37,
          "end": 91.86,
          "en": "and there we can add a new function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 91.86,
          "end": 94.92,
          "en": "The exact position in this file, of course doesn't matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 94.92,
          "end": 96.3,
          "en": "I'll add it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 96.3,
          "end": 99.25,
          "en": "which is an async function that should be exported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 100.28999999999999,
          "end": 105.15,
          "en": "which can be named get user from session.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 105.15,
          "end": 108.87,
          "en": "And here I expect to get a request object as an argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 108.87,
          "end": 110.91,
          "en": "a standard web request object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 110.91,
          "end": 114.33,
          "en": "as it's supported by the browser and by no js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 114.33,
          "end": 118.293,
          "en": "And as it's passed to loaders and actions by Remix,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 119.88,
          "end": 122.19,
          "en": "we can then use the session storage here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 122.19,
          "end": 123.99,
          "en": "to again get a session.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 123.99,
          "end": 126.99,
          "en": "but this time we don't call get session",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 126.99,
          "end": 131.25,
          "en": "like this as we did here for creating a new session.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 131.25,
          "end": 134.85,
          "en": "But instead we pass a value to get session to be precise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 134.85,
          "end": 138.57,
          "en": "the cookie header that's attached to the incoming request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 138.57,
          "end": 141.96,
          "en": "We get access to that cookie by using this request object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 141.96,
          "end": 144.84,
          "en": "And then there there will be a headers object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 144.84,
          "end": 149.61,
          "en": "with a get method and there will be a cookie header added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 149.61,
          "end": 151.89,
          "en": "to the incoming request, which contains",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 151.89,
          "end": 154.38,
          "en": "that session cookie that's stored in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 154.38,
          "end": 156.51,
          "en": "Because as mentioned, it will be attached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 156.51,
          "end": 159.003,
          "en": "to all requests sent to the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 160.07999999999998,
          "end": 163.14,
          "en": "So here we get our session by awaiting this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 163.14,
          "end": 165.36,
          "en": "and once we have our session here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 165.36,
          "end": 167.61,
          "en": "we can extract the user ID from it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 167.61,
          "end": 170.253,
          "en": "by using session, get user id.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 171.12,
          "end": 173.85,
          "en": "We know that there should be a user ID inside of it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 173.85,
          "end": 176.07,
          "en": "because we're adding one to the session",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 176.07,
          "end": 178.263,
          "en": "in this create user session function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 179.52,
          "end": 181.59,
          "en": "So here in get user from session",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 181.59,
          "end": 183.54,
          "en": "I'm extracting it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 183.54,
          "end": 185.79,
          "en": "and then we can simply check if we maybe don't",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 185.79,
          "end": 187.83,
          "en": "have a user id.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 187.83,
          "end": 188.79,
          "en": "If that's the case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 188.79,
          "end": 191.1,
          "en": "we know that we don't have a valid session",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 191.1,
          "end": 194.22,
          "en": "because otherwise it would contain this user id.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 194.22,
          "end": 196.02,
          "en": "By the way, Remix will, of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 196.02,
          "end": 198.84,
          "en": "behind the scenes take a look at this cookie",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 198.84,
          "end": 201.3,
          "en": "and decode this cookie, so to say, using that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 201.3,
          "end": 206.01,
          "en": "secret which we used for setting up the session storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 206.01,
          "end": 209.16,
          "en": "So Remix checks whether this is a valid cookie",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 209.16,
          "end": 211.71,
          "en": "then we check if we have that user id.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 211.71,
          "end": 215.43,
          "en": "If we don't, then it's some invalid value in that cookie.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 215.43,
          "end": 218.07,
          "en": "It's definitely not a locked in user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 218.07,
          "end": 220.2,
          "en": "Therefore then we wanna return null",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 220.2,
          "end": 223.23,
          "en": "We would also not have a user ID if no cookie",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 223.23,
          "end": 226.023,
          "en": "was provided at all as part of the request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 227.22,
          "end": 229.47,
          "en": "So in that case, I return null here I",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 229.47,
          "end": 233.7,
          "en": "I exit early from this function and I return null",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 233.7,
          "end": 236.7,
          "en": "as a value for the user I'm trying to retrieve",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 236.7,
          "end": 239.52,
          "en": "because there is no user attached to this session",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 239.52,
          "end": 242.64,
          "en": "because there is no valid session.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 242.64,
          "end": 246.33,
          "en": "If we do have a valid user ID though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 246.33,
          "end": 249.66,
          "en": "we can return that ID instead as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 249.66,
          "end": 253.233,
          "en": "as an identifier for the user that makes up our session.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 254.97,
          "end": 257.94,
          "en": "And back in our marketing loader,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 257.94,
          "end": 261.66,
          "en": "We can therefore now simply return the result",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 261.66,
          "end": 264.07,
          "en": "of calling get user from session",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 265.26,
          "end": 268.323,
          "en": "which is imported from the A dot server file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 269.4,
          "end": 271.05,
          "en": "Now this returns a promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 271.05,
          "end": 274.40999999999997,
          "en": "because it's an asy function and in this function we",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 274.40999999999997,
          "end": 278.07,
          "en": "of course await accessing our session storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 278.07,
          "end": 282.06,
          "en": "So this returns a promise and loaders can return promises.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 282.06,
          "end": 283.77,
          "en": "So just returning that promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 283.77,
          "end": 286.98,
          "en": "from get user from session is fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 286.98,
          "end": 289.47,
          "en": "And therefore, ultimately in the marketing layout",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 289.47,
          "end": 293.76,
          "en": "and all its nested components and routes, we get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 293.76,
          "end": 297.81,
          "en": "to that user id, which we ultimately return here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 297.81,
          "end": 300.543,
          "en": "So the loader data is that user id.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 301.68,
          "end": 303.54,
          "en": "We just have to make sure that we pass this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 303.54,
          "end": 306.75,
          "en": "request object to get user from session.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 306.75,
          "end": 309.75,
          "en": "And for that thankfully we can use this object past",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 309.75,
          "end": 312.48,
          "en": "to loader, past to loader automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 312.48,
          "end": 315.9,
          "en": "by Remix, I mean, which contains a request property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 315.9,
          "end": 318.9,
          "en": "which has this request object as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 318.9,
          "end": 323.253,
          "en": "So we can pass this request value to get user from session.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 324.24,
          "end": 326.91,
          "en": "Well and with that in marketing layout",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 326.91,
          "end": 330.27,
          "en": "and all nested components we get that user ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 330.27,
          "end": 331.533,
          "en": "if we have it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 332.37,
          "end": 335.37,
          "en": "And that of course means that we can, for example, go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 335.37,
          "end": 339,
          "en": "to this main header JSX file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 339,
          "end": 344,
          "en": "And in there we can get our user ID by calling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 344.04,
          "end": 347.853,
          "en": "useLoaderData Imported from Remix Run React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 348.78,
          "end": 351.54,
          "en": "And with that user ID retrieved here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 351.54,
          "end": 355.443,
          "en": "we can render this login link here conditionally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 356.34000000000003,
          "end": 359.67,
          "en": "We can check if not user id.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 359.67,
          "end": 362.67,
          "en": "So if we have no user and only show the log in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 362.67,
          "end": 363.84,
          "en": "link in that case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 363.84,
          "end": 365.46,
          "en": "because if we have a user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 365.46,
          "end": 367.14,
          "en": "then we know the user is logged in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 367.14,
          "end": 369.663,
          "en": "and there's no reason to show the log in link.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 371.31,
          "end": 374.04,
          "en": "Instead, we could check if user ID is set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 374.04,
          "end": 377.46,
          "en": "And then as an alternative to the log in link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 377.46,
          "end": 380.4,
          "en": "we wanna display a logout button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 380.4,
          "end": 382.293,
          "en": "That could be a good alternative.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 383.79,
          "end": 388.68,
          "en": "Now I'll give this button a class name of cta-alt",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 388.68,
          "end": 392.44,
          "en": "for styling purposes and I'll wrap it in a form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 393.33,
          "end": 396.81,
          "en": "because the logout request which we wanna send",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 396.81,
          "end": 398.76,
          "en": "should not be a get request but instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 398.76,
          "end": 401.94,
          "en": "a post or a delete or anything like that request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 401.94,
          "end": 404.52,
          "en": "hence will actually submit a form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 404.52,
